# Fleet roster — one agent Unix user per line (comments and blank lines ignored).
# Installed to /usr/local/share/agentic/fleet-agents by install-host-services.
#
# WHO ACTUALLY READS THIS, as shipped: only `agentic-divergence-check`. It reconciles this list
# against the brain repos actually present on the box and reports drift in EITHER direction — an
# agent on disk but not listed here, or listed here but absent. `kb-sync` and `agentic-monitor`
# deliberately auto-discover agents from disk instead (each accepts an `AGENTS=` override), because
# auto-discovery is the better default for clone-and-run: a fresh adopter gets coverage without
# having to remember to edit a file.
#
# The trade-off, so you can choose deliberately: auto-discovery cannot tell "this agent is gone" from
# "this agent's brain failed to clone", and it silently covers whatever appears. If an uncovered or
# unexpected agent is a security event for you, make the roster authoritative — point kb-sync and
# agentic-monitor at ROSTER_FILE too, and treat a mismatch as a failure rather than a report. That is
# a legitimate hardening choice, not a fix to this file.
#
# Keep it current when you provision or decommission an agent, or the divergence check will report it.
root-agent
